  lineId: guide_5_physics
  speakerOverride: 
  text: Forward Bias subtracts applied V from V0 (q(V0-V)), narrowing depletion so majority carriers flood exponentially across the junction! Reverse Bias adds V (q(V0+V)), widening W so only tiny Is (~2.5 nA) leaks until avalanche breakdown hits at -50V.
